A picture can be a GPU texture: tvg_picture_load_texture, for a WgCanvas.

For Mayfair's GpuView, whose owner draws into a WGPUTexture on the canvas's own device with
WebGPU of their own, to be drawn as a picture in the scene: in order with everything else, clipped,
transformed and faded like any picture, and never copied. A RenderSurface carries the texture in
place of pixels; the WebGPU engine's texture cache makes a view and a bind group for it, rather
than uploading, and releases it rather than destroying it. Other engines can't draw one.

